But note: goal does not require vehicle allocated to shift_candidate_alpha; but we need it for candidate_prepared.

Thus allocate_vehicle_unit shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_beta.

Then attach_task_profile shift_candidate_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (requires candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, route_task_profile_available). After that we have candidate_task_profile_linked.

Then confirm_candidate_preparedness shift_candidate_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (requires candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, candidate_task_profile_linked, not candidate_prepared). Effect candidate_prepared.

Now we need candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_alpha.

To get loading verified, we can use verify_loading_profile_nominal or verify_loading_profile_destination_flag etc. Which one fits? We need candidate_staged_for_loading first? Actually verify_loading_profile_* preconditions include candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate. So we need to stage candidate before verifying loading.

