Effect: transport_leg_loading_authorized.

Thus we need candidate_task_profile_linked for origin_availability_alpha to route_task_profile_alpha at that time. So we need to have task profile linked to origin_availability_alpha when authorizing. So we should keep task profile linked to origin_availability_alpha until after authorization, then we can detach.

Thus we will not detach origin's task profile until after authorization.

Now after authorization, we need to load container onto leg: load_container_onto_leg requires:
- candidate_prepared ?candidate (which candidate? The action uses ?candidate - schedule_candidate? Actually load_container_onto_leg parameters: (?candidate - schedule_candidate ?loading_container - loading_container ?transport_leg - transport_leg). Precondition includes candidate_prepared ?candidate, candidate_transport_leg_linked ?candidate ?transport_leg, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_available ?loading_container, transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg, transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg, not loading_container_loaded ?loading_container.
Effect: loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked.

Thus we need a schedule_candidate (maybe shift_candidate_alpha) that is prepared and linked to transport leg and loading container. We have shift_candidate_alpha prepared, linked to transport_leg_alpha and loading_container_alpha. Good.

